    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$-2\\le x\\le 3$.\n\nSplit into cases at $x=-1$ and $x=2$, where the expressions inside the absolute values change sign.",
      "worked": "For $x<-1$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}-(x+1)-(x-2)&\\le 5\\\\-2x+1&\\le 5\\\\x&\\ge -2\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis gives $-2\\le x<-1$.\n\nFor $-1\\le x\\le 2$, the sum is $(x+1)+(2-x)=3$, so every value in this interval satisfies the inequality.\n\nFor $x>2$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(x+1)+(x-2)&\\le 5\\\\2x-1&\\le 5\\\\x&\\le 3\\end{align*}$$\n\nThis gives $2<x\\le 3$. Combining the three cases gives $\\boxed{-2\\le x\\le 3}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 100
  },
